# ============================================================================
# Secrets — NEVER committed. (PROJECT_RULES.md Door 3 / secrets custody.)
# The most permanent secret in the system is the email-hash pepper; losing it
# de-joins all history, leaking it makes low-entropy addresses brute-forceable.
# It, node tokens, vendor keys, and Supabase keys are loaded from secure config
# at runtime and are never present in the repo. See config/secrets.example.env.
# ============================================================================
*.env
.env
.env.*
!*.example.env
# A secrets STORE directory (real key/pepper material) — anchored so it does NOT match the Go
# SOURCE package control-plane/internal/secrets/ (which is code, never secret material, and MUST
# be tracked or a fresh clone won't compile). The unanchored `secrets/` previously swallowed that
# package silently. Real secrets are still blocked by *.env / *.pem / *.key / *.pepper below.
/secrets/
/config/secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.pepper
config/secrets.env
config/local.*.yaml

# Go (control-plane)
/control-plane/bin/
/control-plane/dist/
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html

# Ruby (verifier-node / forked truemail-rack)
verifier-node/**/.bundle/
verifier-node/**/vendor/bundle/
verifier-node/**/tmp/
verifier-node/**/coverage/
verifier-node/**/log/
*.gem

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Build / CI artifacts
/artifacts/
/.task-cache/
